 begins in new york city  where she lives with her husband  the same day that the manhattan  quarantine was put in place she went to  visit her husband at work  where she had to watch him from a  distance be gunned down in front of his  office  by unknown men dressed in black  stuck on the island because of the  quarantine she roamed the area  not just trying to survive but looking  for clues on why her husband was  murdered  writing in a book she was gifted by her  husband called new york collapse  a survival guide to urban catastrophe  she wrote down her thoughts  and experiences april talks about the  state of the city  and her confusion around his death she  also describes a number of different  events where she had come into contact  with rikers  in both division and rogue agents  including aaron kina  over time she witnessed a number of  friends succumbed to the events that  occurred  as well as the virus she goes into  detail around the time that she too  contracted an illness that resembled the  dole flow  and survived eventually april finds  someone deep inside the dark zone by the  name of merch  who knows of her husband and what he was  working on  he was responsible for his part in the  development of a class of vaccines  known as broad-spectrum antivirals a  type of vaccine that could help fight  against all strains of the green poison  this work led him to being killed for  his involvement by an unknown  organization  merch tells april that there is a lab in  ann arbor that is currently working on  the antivirals  and had worked with her husband april  decides to make her way to the lab  to take a look at what he'd given his  life for  outside of the major cities april runs  into a number of different groups  mostly just people doing their best to  survive during this time  but she certainly ran into a few who  were taking advantage of the current  situation  and in one such situation just outside  ann arbor  she was rescued by shd agent ike ronson  from a group of criminals  when they made it to the city they  decided to rest before visiting the labs  the next day  camping out on a rooftop cafe they were  met by another shd agent  aurelio diaz  the next day the three of them visited  the research facility and talked with  the head researcher  who confirms that they have in fact been  working on the broad spectrum antivirals  it was during this time that diaz  received a call it was revealed that  ronson has been working as a double  agent  for an organization called the black  tusk  ronson was a rogue agent  although diaz managed to subdue ronson  it was too late  the cavalry was on its way a full-scale  black tusk attack was fast approaching  the compound  april and diaz leave him behind and  managed to escape through a forest  nearby  and this is where they're part ways  april heads off to washington dc  to tell them of what she had witnessed  while diaz decided to head east  and do what he could to put a stop to  this new invading force  so from this what do we have civilians  doctors scientists laboratory workers  black tusk agents rogues anti-virals  and a free-to-play game now let's be  fair free to play could mean any number  of things  but if it is in fact based in michigan  we have a few decent factors here that  could make up a pretty fun game  with a solid story to back it up i need  to state right now that i've had  absolutely no contact with the  developers working on this or anyone  involved  actually now that i think of it i don't  think i've ever had a response from them  oh well what i'm trying to say is i have  absolutely no inside knowledge of what's  going on  and that what i'm about to talk about is  simply my own ideas around what this  game could be  with that out of the way picture this a  dark zone  pve vp survival last stand zone control  hybrid  hear me out we have a map of ann arbor  including some of the rural space around  it and although there is likely to be a  number of smaller activities involved  throughout  the overarching mission is to gain  control of the city  there is the shd agents the black tusk  potentially the ai faction  and the rogues they are all fighting for  control of ann arbor  with the main research facility being  located in the middle of the map i  probably need to bring up some visuals  to better explain the craziness going on  in my head  apologies i'm not hugely familiar with  ann arbor's district zoning  this was just something i quickly threw  together  in the center we have the research  facility civilians are scattered  throughout  as you'd expect it's a city after all  each of the factions have their own home  location or starting point  an area that cannot be captured by the  opposing factions  the area outside of these home locations  are also generally assumed to be kept  under control  due to the faction influence or fear and  have support from the civilians located  there  making it harder to lose or be captured  by opposing factions  as factions get further away from their  home locations it gets more difficult  and requires more effort and  coordination to capture districts  also district control can be lost not  just by other factions  but due to the civilian occupation not  being kept happy  this could be a short round-based battle  or a long-term beast  where it takes considerable time to  capture a district with a potential  ladder reset every now and then  this would be a game type where the pvp  and pve  are just as important yes you're coming  up against opposing human players on one  front  but equally there is an npc battle going  on over the other side  that needs to be kept in check plus  there are civilians in each district  that need to be kept happy  or they will revolt the centre of the  map holds the overall goal  and although you can run into any  uncontrolled district freely when not  under the control of your faction  the people here will be considerably  more hostile towards you  on the other side when traveling through  an area under your faction's control  there will be support from the civilians  and militia groups as well as restocks  and potentially vendors however gaining  control of the regions around the  central research facility  will gain weapons and equipment and  glory points for your faction  at a greater rate than what could be  acquired anywhere else on the map  this game mode would need to include a  large number of players to do it justice  not just the usual 8 or 12 players  or maybe heartlands would just be  another bloody battle royale  so this is all fairly unlikely to happen  but i still think it would be pretty  cool  it's certainly something i'd be keen on  playing well done if you've made it this  far listening to me neteron about my  random ideas  my wife was getting sick of hearing  about them so i had to tell someone  i have so many more but i think i'll  have to try and restrain from talking  about them too much  like my ideas around the mobile game and  how they could use augmented reality to  create something a little more  interesting  than most of us are probably imagining  they'll produce  i should totally get into game  development if i actually had any  tangible skills to bring to the table  okay i'm rambling again anyway thank you  very much for watching  and i'll catch in the next one cheers  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  thank you

